          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the ground is already open, seal the exterior with a <strong class="text-white">liquid rubber membrane</strong> and protect it with a drainage board — nothing else comes close. Working from inside, <strong class="text-white">DRYLOK Extreme</strong> is the strongest coating for a damp wall, <strong class="text-white">Ames Blue Max</strong> is the one for a wall that cracks or never dries, and <strong class="text-white">RadonSeal</strong> is the permanent answer on dense poured concrete.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Before any of that, spend an afternoon on the gutters, the downspouts and the grade. Those three fix more wet foundations than every product on this page combined, and they cost almost nothing — which makes them the only sensible place to start.
          </p>
